# SPA fallback for the client-only category-filter routes /projects/<tag> ONLY.
#
# DO NOT use a /projects/* splat. On Cloudflare Pages a 200-rewrite takes
# precedence OVER static assets, so "/projects/*  /  200" rewrote EVERY
# /projects/... request — projects-config.json, per-project JSON/HTML/images,
# and the prerendered /projects/<slug> pages — to the home shell, breaking the
# Projects list ("Unexpected token '<'") and every project detail page.
#
# Tags, project slugs and real files all live at /projects/<one-segment>, so we
# must list the (non-prerendered, non-file) tag routes explicitly. Every other
# path has no matching rule and correctly falls through to its static asset.
#
# Keep in sync with PROJECT_TAGS in src/components/utils/projectUtils.js.
# Target "/projects/" WITH the trailing slash: it is the canonical 200 URL of the
# prerendered projects-list page, so CF serves it as a clean in-place 200 rewrite
# (the address bar stays /projects/<tag>) and the SPA reads the slug to apply the
# filter. A target of "/projects" (no slash) instead 308-redirects to "/projects/",
# dropping the tag from the URL and losing the filter on a hard load / shared link.
/projects/master           /projects/  200
/projects/bachelor         /projects/  200
/projects/data-science     /projects/  200
/projects/explainable-ai   /projects/  200
/projects/hackathon        /projects/  200
/projects/business         /projects/  200
/projects/volunteering     /projects/  200
/projects/web-development  /projects/  200
